<title>FRANCE: European single currency must begin on time - Bruton.</title>
<headline>European single currency must begin on time - Bruton.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish Prime Minister John Bruton said European economic and monetary union must begin in 1999 as foreseen in the Maastricht treaty, according to a speech released ahead of delivery on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Economic and monetary union must commence on time, and in line with treaty requirements,&quot; Bruton said in a speech destined for delivery to the European Parliament.</p>
<p>The single market, if it is to be consolidated, must be underpinned by a strong and stable European currency, he said.</p>
</text>
